\pard\b 16. Firewall planning\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Open only the inbound services this site needs, using the product checklist as the source of truth.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Before you start\par
\pard 1. Know who owns host firewall rules and who owns upstream firewall rules.\par
\pard 2. Know whether the site is LAN-Only or WAN Public Edge.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Sign in as super administrator.\par
\pard 2. Open the firewall readiness / inbound services checklist in Settings (Diagnostics or Cloud Deployment checklist area when shown).\par
\pard 3. For each required row, create a matching allow rule on the host firewall.\par
\pard 4. Repeat on upstream firewalls for the networks that must reach the server (control room, camera VLAN, VPN as designed).\par
\pard 5. Do not publish Setup (13988) beyond the server itself.\par
\pard 6. For LAN-Only, restrict operator and camera sources to private ranges whenever policy allows.\par
\pard 7. For WAN Public Edge, publish only the reverse-proxy HTTPS front door and the camera/media ports your design requires. Keep Setup closed.\par
\pard 8. Record rules in the site runbook with the date and the Settings values used.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Checklist ports that are required for your license and features are open from the correct source networks. Setup remains local.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Planning worksheet (fill with your values)\par
\pard 1. Operator portal URL: ____________________\par
\pard 2. Device registration IPv4: ____________________\par
\pard 3. SIP port: ____________________\par
\pard 4. Dashboard listen port: ____________________\par
\pard 5. Camera source networks: ____________________\par
\pard 6. Operator source networks: ____________________\par
\pard 7. Reverse proxy host (if any): ____________________\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Common problems\par
\pard 1. Host firewall updated but upstream firewall forgotten.\par
\pard 2. SIP port changed in Settings but firewall still allows only the old port.\par
\pard 3. RTP media range not opened \emdash register works, live video fails.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Inbound services checklist]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 17. Evidence storage and FTP\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Configure where evidence files are stored and, when used, how docks and cameras upload by FTP.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Before you start\par
\pard 1. If you use NAS or SAN, mount it on the server operating system first and confirm the path is writable by the service account.\par
\pard 2. Super administrator access is required to change storage.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps \emdash storage paths\par
\pard 1. Open Evidence \emdash Storage (super administrator).\par
\pard 2. Review IP SAN / NAS mount status if applicable.\par
\pard 3. Set upload paths for dock FTP and live capture as required by your design.\par
\pard 4. Understand that the evidence index (catalog) stays on the server while video archive files follow the archive path you set.\par
\pard 5. Save storage settings.\par
\pard 6. Use path test / status badges when available to confirm Ready or Mounted.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps \emdash FTP ingest (when used)\par
\pard 1. In Evidence storage, open FTP upload service settings.\par
\pard 2. Enable FTP ingest if docks or cameras upload by FTP.\par
\pard 3. Set FTP password and related credentials. Enter the same values on each device FTP screen.\par
\pard 4. Save FTP settings. Restart if the product reports that the FTP service restarted.\par
\pard 5. Open firewall rows for FTP control and passive data ranges from the live checklist when FTP is enabled.\par
\pard 6. Run an upload test from one dock or camera and confirm the file appears in the configured folder and index.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Evidence paths are writable. FTP devices authenticate. Files appear for operators according to their rights.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard 1. Mobility Axiom writes to the folders you configure. It does not replace OS-level NAS mounting.\par
\pard 2. Backup of evidence media and the install folder is a site policy task. Schedule it after go-live.\par
\pard 3. Password may not be shown again after save. Store device FTP credentials in your vault.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Common problems\par
\pard 1. Path Not found or Read-only \emdash fix OS mount and permissions.\par
\pard 2. FTP enabled in product but passive port range closed on firewall.\par
\pard 3. Device FTP password out of sync after a credential rotation.\par
\pard\sa120\par
