\pard\b 18. Supporting services (container engine)\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Explain how Mobility Axiom relates to the optional container engine used for some supporting services, what must stay running, and what IT checks when those services fail.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 18.1 Plain model\par
\pard Mobility Axiom itself runs as a normal Windows Server or Linux service. That service is the main product: dashboard, Settings, licensing, camera registration values, evidence paths, and operator access.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Some supporting components for certain site designs run as containers managed by a container engine (commonly called Docker Engine on Linux Server, or Docker Desktop on some Windows deliveries). The delivery package may include a docker configuration folder. That folder is not the same thing as installing the engine on the operating system.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Important\par
\pard 1. Operators never manage the container engine.\par
\pard 2. IT does not start containers by hand every morning on a correct production install.\par
\pard 3. When supporting containers are part of the site design, the engine and those containers must start at boot and stay running in the background.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 18.2 When the container engine is required\par
\pard Use your contract, license entitlements, and package README for this order. Typical cases:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\b Required\par
\pard 1. Video Conference is licensed and this package hosts conference services in containers.\par
\pard 2. Your Ubitron delivery states that live media helpers for this site run as supporting containers.\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard\b Not required for core alone\par
\pard Dashboard login, Setup, license install, Server Config, user accounts, and evidence path configuration do not require IT to open a container console every day.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard If Ubitron delivered a pre-built server image where the engine and required containers already auto-start, you may never open a container UI during normal operations. Still keep this chapter for recovery.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 18.3 What must run in the background\par
\pard\b Steps \emdash production expectation\par
\pard 1. Install or confirm the container engine according to the package README for this order (or confirm the Ubitron appliance image already includes it).\par
\pard 2. Configure the engine to start when the server starts.\par
\pard 3. Start the supporting containers named in the README for this site.\par
\pard 4. Confirm those containers are set to restart automatically after reboot.\par
\pard 5. Confirm the Mobility Axiom server service is also set to start automatically.\par
\pard 6. Reboot once during commissioning and verify: Mobility Axiom service Running, required containers running, Operator portal opens, and licensed Video Conference or live media checks succeed.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard After a cold reboot, both the Mobility Axiom service and the required supporting containers return without manual clicks.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard 1. On some Windows deliveries the engine is Docker Desktop. Enable start with Windows and wait until the engine reports ready after boot before testing conference or media helpers.\par
\pard 2. On Linux Server, prefer the native Docker Engine service (or the runtime named in the README), enabled for boot.\par
\pard 3. Prefer pre-staged images from Ubitron for air-gap sites. Do not treat public internet image pulls as the primary enterprise method unless your cover letter says otherwise.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 18.4 Relationship to Device registration IPv4\par
\pard\b Warning\par
\pard Never use virtual adapter addresses in the range 172.17 to 172.31 as Device registration IPv4 or as operator bookmarks. Container and virtualisation adapters commonly use those ranges. Cameras must use the server real LAN (or designed) IPv4 from Networking / Type on BWC.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 18.5 IT checks when supporting services fail\par
\pard\b Before you start\par
\pard Confirm the symptom: Video Conference will not start, or live media helpers fail while the Mobility Axiom service itself is Running.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Confirm the Mobility Axiom service is Running.\par
\pard 2. Confirm the container engine is running.\par
\pard 3. Confirm the containers listed in the package README for this site are running (not stopped or restarting in a loop).\par
\pard 4. Restart only the failed supporting containers using the README procedure, then retest.\par
\pard 5. If Engine was stopped, start Engine, wait until ready, confirm containers, then retest.\par
\pard 6. Recheck firewall rows for the licensed module (for example conference ports) from the live checklist.\par
\pard 7. If still failing, capture Mobility Axiom logs plus container status names from the README and contact Ubitron.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Licensed conference or media helpers work again without reinstalling Mobility Axiom.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Common problems\par
\pard 1. Engine set not to start at boot \emdash works until the first reboot.\par
\pard 2. Mobility Axiom service Running but conference containers stopped \emdash portal works, conference fails.\par
\pard 3. IT uses a container virtual address as Device registration IPv4 \emdash cameras fail.\par
\pard\sa120\par
