\pard\b 19. Optional licensed modules\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Understand that some modules appear only when your license includes them.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Depending on entitlement, the product may offer modules such as:\par
\pard 1. PTT\par
\pard 2. Redaction\par
\pard 3. Analytics (for example face, plate, or weapon analytics as licensed)\par
\pard 4. Video conference\par
\pard 5. Tactical overwatch\par
\pard 6. \b CAD / RMS\b0  (Computer-Aided Dispatch / Records Management) \emdash optional integration\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps for IT\par
\pard 1. After license install, open the product and note which modules are available versus locked.\par
\pard 2. For available modules, complete any module-specific Settings and firewall rows from the live checklist.\par
\pard 3. For Video Conference and any module that depends on supporting containers, complete Chapter 18 before operator handoff.\par
\pard 4. For \b CAD / RMS\b0 , confirm the optional integration entitlement is present before operators rely on that tab.\par
\pard 5. For locked modules, contact Ubitron to change the license. Do not attempt to bypass locks.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard Follow the package README for module-specific host steps. Chapter 18 covers the container engine pattern used by several supporting stacks. After first mention in this manual, the tab is written as \b CAD / RMS\b0 .\par
