\pard\b Part D \emdash Operations and recovery\par
\pard\sa240\par

\pard\b 20. Service operations\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Start, stop, and restart Mobility Axiom safely.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Windows Server\par
\pard 1. Open Services.\par
\pard 2. Locate the Mobility Axiom server service.\par
\pard 3. Use Start, Stop, or Restart.\par
\pard 4. Confirm Startup type remains Automatic (or the value required by the README).\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Linux\par
\pard 1. Use systemctl to start, stop, restart, and status the unit named in your package README.\par
\pard 2. Confirm the unit is enabled for boot.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b When restart is mandatory\par
\pard 1. After network or SIP changes in Server Config\par
\pard 2. After listen-port changes from the package README\par
\pard 3. After certain FTP service credential changes when the product reports a restart\par
\pard 4. After recovering from license or clock faults that required Setup\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard Restarting Mobility Axiom does not always restart supporting containers. If conference or media helpers stay down after an app restart, use Chapter 18.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Service returns to Running / active. Dashboard login responds. Cameras can re-register.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Service Running after restart]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 21. Logs and what to capture for support\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Collect the right evidence when you escalate to Ubitron.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Where to look\par
\pard 1. Windows: service log file under the install folder (path in the README)\par
\pard 2. Linux: journalctl for the service unit, or the log path in the README\par
\pard 3. Additional operational logs under the install storage area as named in the README\par
\pard 4. When supporting containers are involved: container names and status from the package README procedure\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b What to send\par
\pard 1. Customer and site name\par
\pard 2. Contract or purchase order reference\par
\pard 3. Hardware ID\par
\pard 4. Server OS and version\par
\pard 5. Package version from the delivery README\par
\pard 6. Short description of expected versus actual behaviour\par
\pard 7. Recent service log excerpt (remove secrets if policy requires)\par
\pard 8. Supporting container status when the fault is conference or media-helper related\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard If the log shows a structured fault with what happened, why, and how to fix, include that full block and follow How to fix first.\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 22. Start-up and runtime recovery\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b 22.1 Cannot open Setup\par
\pard 1. Confirm the service is running.\par
\pard 2. Browse on the server or tunnel to localhost.\par
\pard 3. Read the service log for Setup port and bind errors.\par
\pard 4. Free the port if another process owns it, then restart.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.2 No Setup PIN\par
\pard 1. Search the log for Setup Mode or ACTION REQUIRED.\par
\pard 2. Restart once and search again.\par
\pard 3. Confirm you are reading the log for this install path.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.3 Port already in use\par
\pard 1. Identify which port the log names.\par
\pard 2. Stop the conflicting application or follow the README to select an alternate port.\par
\pard 3. Restart Mobility Axiom.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.4 Hardware clock / date and time\par
\pard If the server clock is wrong (especially stuck in the past), the product may refuse a normal start until BIOS/UEFI and operating system time are corrected and time sync is restored. Fix time first, then restart the service.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.5 License rejected\par
\pard Confirm Hardware ID match, do not edit the file, contact Ubitron with the error text.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.6 Structured how-to-fix log blocks\par
\pard When the service log shows a structured fault with three lines (what happened / why / how to fix), follow How to fix before opening a support case. Ubitron support may ask you for that log block.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.7 Service will not stay running\par
\pard 1. Check date and time.\par
\pard 2. Check port conflicts.\par
\pard 3. Read how-to-fix lines in the log.\par
\pard 4. Confirm the license is still present.\par
\pard 5. Escalate with log excerpt if unresolved.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b 22.8 Supporting containers down\par
\pard See Chapter 18. Confirm engine running, required containers running, then retest the licensed module.\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 23. Camera and SIP path check (advanced IT)\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Purpose\par
\pard Verify that cameras and the server agree on registration address and port after networking changes.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. In Settings, copy Device registration IPv4 and SIP port from Type on BWC.\par
\pard 2. On one camera, confirm the same IPv4 and SIP port are programmed.\par
\pard 3. Confirm the camera network can route to that IPv4.\par
\pard 4. Confirm firewall allows BWC SIP and required media ports from the camera network.\par
\pard 5. Restart the camera radio or power-cycle once.\par
\pard 6. Confirm Online in Mobility Axiom.\par
\pard 7. Open one live view.\par
\pard 8. If registration succeeds but live video fails, re-check media/RTP firewall rows, media transport setting, and Chapter 18 if your site uses supporting media containers.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b When to escalate\par
\pard If one known-good camera still fails after IP, SIP port, password, routing, and firewall all match Type on BWC, collect logs and contact Ubitron. Do not invent alternate ports from another site.\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 24. Go-live acceptance checklist\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard Confirm each item before you declare the site ready for operators:\par
\pard\sa80\par
\pard 1. Mobility Axiom service is Running / active and set to start automatically.\par
\pard 2. License is accepted; Setup is not required for daily start.\par
\pard 3. Administrator password changed; factory password rejected.\par
\pard 4. Operator portal URL opens from a control-room workstation.\par
\pard 5. Device registration IPv4 is the real LAN (or designed) address \emdash not 172.17 to 172.31.\par
\pard 6. At least one body-worn camera shows Online.\par
\pard 7. At least one live view succeeds.\par
\pard 8. Evidence storage path is Ready or Mounted and a test file can be stored or uploaded.\par
\pard 9. Firewall rules match the live checklist for required services.\par
\pard 10. Setup is not published to the public internet.\par
\pard 11. Operator accounts exist for dispatch staff.\par
\pard 12. If this order uses supporting containers: engine starts at boot and required containers are running after a reboot test (Chapter 18).\par
\pard 13. Site runbook lists portal URL, SIP port, restart procedure, and Ubitron support contact.\par
\pard 14. Quick Start Guide and User Manual are issued to operators.\par
\pard\sa120\par
